-\draftnote{This section specifies the proposed confirmatory procedure. The implemented snapshot supports one practice trial, two 40-trial blocks, and a final questionnaire handoff. Exact pre-cue geometry, vertical balancing, sample size, and pilot acceptance rules remain unresolved, as detailed in Appendix~\ref{app:readiness}.}
+\draftnote{This section specifies the proposed confirmatory procedure. The implemented snapshot supports one practice trial, two 40-trial blocks, and a final questionnaire handoff. Exact pre-cue geometry, vertical balancing, sample size, and pilot acceptance rules remain unresolved.}
 \subsection{Voice Manipulation and Comparison Rationale}
 The method compares two ways of personalizing assistance: a synthetic voice derived from the participant's recorded speech and a neutral voice selected by that participant from the supplied catalog. Letting participants choose the neutral alternative ties the comparison to a design choice a user could face, while the within-participant task provides repeated observations under both configurations. Similarity ratings will indicate whether participants heard the clone as resembling themselves, whereas performance and experience measures will compare how each voice functions as guidance.
 
